0000:                   * krnp2 - NitrOS-9 Level 2 Kernel Part 2
0000:                   *
0000:                   * $Id$
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Copyright (c) 1982 Microware Corporation
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Modified for 6309 Native mode by:
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Bill Nobel, L. Curtis Boyle & Wes Gale - Gale Force Enterprises
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Ed.    Comments                                       Who YY/MM/DD
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *
0000:                   * 17.2   08/02/92 - Active in 6309 Native mode, No apparent bugs (BN)
0000:                   *                 - Optimized F$Fork (BN)
0000:                   *                 - Optimized F$Chain (BN)
0000:                   * 18.4   92/12/15 - Cut initial memory allocation routine - unnecessary
0000:                   * 18.5   93/01/18 - Fixed bug in F$Sleep (LCB)
0000:                   *                 - Optimized F$All64 to use tfm (BN)
0000:                   * NitrOS9 V1.09 - Move & optimized F$CpyMem to OS9P1
0000:                   * V1.10  93/05/23 - Slight opt to UnLink
0000:                   * V1.11  93/07/26 - Slight opt in F$Icpt
0000:                   *                 - Slight opt in F$Wait alarm clearing
0000:                   *                 - Slight opt to speed up path table full errors
0000:                   *                 - Changed LBEQ to BEQ in F$Unlink
0000:                   * V1.16  93/09/03 - Moved F$SUser to OS9P1 (WG)
0000:                   *        93/09/08 - Moved F$SUser back to OS9P2 for room in OS9P1 (LCB)
0000:                   *        93/09/10 - F$Find64 (L0A50) - Took out BSR to L0A5C, merged routine
0000:                   *                   in (only called from here), and took out PSHS/PULS D
0000:                   *                   Also modified error structure a bit to shorten it
0000:                   *        93/10/06 - Added conditional assembly to skip Network I/O ptrs since
0000:                   *                   Coco network never released by Tandy/Microware (in F$Fork)
0000:                   *                 - @ GotNProc (in F$Fork), saved 1 byte/cycle when inheriting
0000:                   *                   User # & priority
0000:                   *                 - Changed routine @ L01FB to use U instead of Y (slightly
0000:                   *                   smaller & slightly faster), and also used CLRB with STB
0000:                   *                   instead of CLR for clearing DAT block #'s (F$UnLink)
0000:                   *        93/12/17 - Moved F$CRCMod code here to give some room in OS9P1
0000:                   *        94/05/15 - Attempted opts in Unlink: Changed usage of W to D @ L0185
0000:                   *                   and L0198 and L01B5, also optimized L017C to eliminate a
0000:                   *                   branch (speeds up module dir search by 3 cycles/module
0000:                   *                   checked)
0000:                   *                 - Changed BRA L032F @ L02EC (AllProc error) to RTS
0000:                   *                 - Changed BRA L0629 @ L05DF to RTS
0000:                   *                 - Changed L066A & L067B from BRA L06F4 to PULS CC,A,Y,U,PC
0000:                   *                   (F$Send errors)
0000:                   *                 - Changed L0A2B from BRA L0A4F to RTS (F$UnLoad error)
0000:                   *                 - Changed L0C53 & L0C81 BRA L0C93 to CLRB/RTS (F$GCMDir)
0000:                   * -- Alan DeKok
0000:                   *        94/10/28 - added boot debug calls
0000:                   *                 - Changed code at ~L0D47 to allow F$Fork/F$Chain of Obj6309
0000:                   *        94/10/30 - Added error checking on F$Fork of CC3Go
0000:                   *                 - Minor mods to F$SSWI call
0000:                   *                 - Minor mods to F$STime
0000:                   *                 - Changed F$GModDr to BRA to similar code in F$GBlkMp
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  18r6  Back-ported to OS-9 Level Two from NitrOS-9 Level Two
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  18r7    2004/06/18  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * Kernel no longer attempts a reboot when failing to open term device, but
0000:                   * crashes upon error.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  19      2013/05/29  Boisy G. Pitre
0000:                   * F$Debug now incorporated, allows for reboot.
0000:                   
0000:                            nam    krnp2
0000:                            ttl    NitrOS-9 Level 2 Kernel Part 2
